LICENSING NOTE

1. Data (data/*.json): words, definitions, translations and example sentences

The data was generated automatically from these sources and keeps their licences:

- English, French, Spanish and Russian Wiktionary, via Wiktextract / kaikki.org.
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
- FLELex (CENTAL, UCLouvain). French CEFR levels.
  Licence: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/
- KELLY Russian word list (University of Leeds). Russian CEFR levels.
  Licence: CC BY-NC-SA 2.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/
- SMARTool data-rus-eng (UiT The Arctic University of Norway). Russian CEFR levels.
  Licence: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
- Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org), weekly exports. Example sentences and their Spanish/English translations;
  each sentence carries its Tatoeba ID (https://tatoeba.org/sentences/show/<ID>).
  Licence: CC BY 2.0 FR, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/
- Open Multilingual Wordnet 1.4. Used only to score translation reliability.
  Licences: WordNet 3.0 licence, CeCILL-C, CC BY 3.0 and CC BY-SA 4.0 (one per wordnet).

The compiled data set is therefore distributed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0: attribution required, non-commercial use only, and adaptations must be shared under the same terms. The individual Wiktionary-derived parts also remain available under CC BY-SA 4.0. Full attributions and citations are in data/credits.json and on the app's About screen.

